                    "value": 135,
                    "readOnly": false
                },
                {
                    "name": "Motor rated current",
                    "index": "#x6075",
                    "sub_index": "",
                    "unit": "mA",
                    "min": 1,
                    "max": 1000000,
                    "defaultData": 1,
                    "mandatory": false,
                    "description": "<p>The motor rated current is taken from the motor datasheet. It needs to be configured in rms value. In the datasheet it could be defined in other units (peak value), therefore it needs to be converted into rms value before configuration. The units are in Milliampere [mA]. All relative current data refers to this value (such as <code>0x6073 Max current</code>).</p>",
                    "inputType": "number",
                    "isSmm": false,
                    "bitSize": 32,
                    "esiType": "UDINT",
                    "canBeMappedAsRxPdo": false,
                    "canBeMappedAsTxPdo": false,
                    "recordDescription": "",
                    "options": "",
                    "group": "",
                    "typeValue": "",
                    "originalOptions": "",
                    "value": 13100,
                    "readOnly": false
                },
                {
                    "name": "Motor rated torque",
                    "index": "#x6076",
                    "sub_index": "",
                    "unit": "mNm",
                    "min": 1,
                    "max": 4294967295,
                    "defaultData": 1,
                    "mandatory": false,
                    "description": "<p>Indicates the nominal torque for the motor. It is taken from the motor's specifications. All relative torque data shall refer to this value (such as <code>0x6072 Max torque</code>). For linear motors, the object name is not changed, but the motor rated force value must be entered as multiples of mN (millinewton). The value shall be given in mNm (millinewton metre).</p>",
                    "inputType": "number",
                    "isSmm": false,
                    "bitSize": 32,
                    "esiType": "UDINT",
                    "canBeMappedAsRxPdo": false,
                    "canBeMappedAsTxPdo": false,
                    "recordDescription": "",
                    "options": "",
                    "group": "",
                    "typeValue": "",
                    "originalOptions": "",
                    "value": 660,
                    "readOnly": false
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "parameters": [
                {
                    "name": "Max torque",
                    "index": "#x6072",
                    "sub_index": "",
                    "unit": "",
                    "min": 0,
                    "max": 32767,
                    "defaultData": 3000,
                    "mandatory": false,
                    "description": "<p>The configured maximum permissible torque in the motor. The value is given in per thousandth of rated torque.</p>\r\n\t<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mi>Max Torque</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <msub><mi>&tau;</mi><mi>max_Datasheet</mi></msub> <msub><mi>&tau;</mi><mi>rated_Datasheet</mi></msub> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mi>1000</mi> </mrow> </math></p>\r\n\t<p>For example, if the rated torque from the datasheet is 200 Nm and maximum torque is 600 Nm,</p>\r\n\t<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Max Torque </mi> <mo>= </mo><mfrac><mi>600 Nm </mi><mi>200 Nm </mi> </mfrac> <mo>&times; </mo> <mi>1000 </mi> <mo>= </mo> <mi>3000 </mi> </mrow> </math></p>",
                    "inputType": "number",
                    "isSmm": false,
                    "bitSize": 16,
                    "esiType": "UINT",
                    "canBeMappedAsRxPdo": true,
                    "canBeMappedAsTxPdo": false,
                    "recordDescription": "",
                    "options": "",
                    "group": "",
                    "typeValue": "",
                    "originalOptions": "",
                    "value": 3787,
                    "readOnly": false
                },
                {
                    "name": "Max current",
                    "index": "#x6073",
                    "sub_index": "",
                    "unit": "",
                    "min": 0,
                    "max": 50000,
                    "defaultData": 3000,
                    "mandatory": false,
                    "description": "<p>Indicates the configured maximum permissible torque-creating current in the motor. The units are per thousand of rated current.</p>\r\n\t<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mi>Max Current</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <msub><mi>I</mi><mi>max_Datasheet</mi></msub> <msub><mi>I</mi><mi>rated_Datasheet</mi></msub> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mi>1000</mi> </mrow> </math></p>\r\n\t<p>For example, if the <code>0x6075 Motor rated current</code> is 2 Amps and maximum current which can be applied for short duration is 6 Amps,</p>\r\n\t<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>Max Current </mi> <mo>= </mo><mfrac><mi>6 Amps </mi><mi>2 Amps </mi> </mfrac> <mo>&times; </mo> <mi>1000 </mi> <mo>= </mo> <mi>3000 </mi> </mrow> </math></p>",
                    "inputType": "number",
                    "isSmm": false,
                    "bitSize": 16,
                    "esiType": "UINT",
                    "canBeMappedAsRxPdo": true,
                    "canBeMappedAsTxPdo": false,
                    "recordDescription": "",
                    "options": "",
                    "group": "",
                    "typeValue": "",
                    "originalOptions": "",
                    "value": 4245,
                    "readOnly": false
                },
                {
                    "name": "Max motor speed",
                    "index": "#x6080",
                    "sub_index": "",
                    "unit": "rpm",
                    "min": 0,
                    "max": 4294967295,
                    "defaultData": 1000,
                    "mandatory": false,
                    "description": "<p>Sets the max allowed speed for the motor in either direction. It is used to protect the motor and is taken from the motor data sheet. The value shall be given in RPM by default (see <code>0x60a9 SI unit velocity</code> to change it).</p>",
                    "inputType": "number",
                    "isSmm": false,
                    "bitSize": 32,
                    "esiType": "UDINT",
                    "canBeMappedAsRxPdo": true,
                    "canBeMappedAsTxPdo": false,
                    "recordDescription": "",
                    "options": "",
                    "group": "",
                    "typeValue": "",
                    "originalOptions": "",
                    "value": 9000,
                    "readOnly": false
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "parameters": [
                {
                    "name": "Motor revolutions",
                    "index": "#x6091",
                    "sub_index": "01",
                    "unit": "",
                    "min": 0,
                    "max": 4294967295,
                    "defaultData": 1,
                    "mandatory": true,
                    "description": "<p>Defines the ratio of motor shaft revolutions to driving shaft revolutions. The term <em>driving shaft</em> refers to the shaft where the encoder used for position control is mounted. If no position control encoder is used, it refers to the shaft where the encoder used for velocity control is mounted.</p>\r\n<p>If there is only one encoder configured, or if the encoder used for position control is on the motor shaft, this parameter is not used. To scale the position between the driving shaft and the output of a gearbox, 0x6092 Feed constant should be used to create a virtual gear ratio instead.</p>\r\n<p>All values for this parameter are dimensionless.</p>",
                    "inputType": "number",
                    "isSmm": false,
                    "bitSize": 64,
                    "esiType": "DT6091ARR",
                    "canBeMappedAsRxPdo": true,
                    "canBeMappedAsTxPdo": false,
                    "recordDescription": "",
                    "options": "",
                    "group": "Gear ratio",
                    "typeValue": "",
                    "originalOptions": "",
                    "value": 1,
                    "readOnly": false
                },
                {
                    "name": "Shaft revolutions",
                    "index": "#x6091",
                    "sub_index": "02",
                    "unit": "",
                    "min": 0,
                    "max": 4294967295,
                    "defaultData": 1,
                    "mandatory": true,
                    "description": "<p>Defines the ratio of motor shaft revolutions to driving shaft revolutions. The term <em>driving shaft</em> refers to the shaft where the encoder used for position control is mounted. If no position control encoder is used, it refers to the shaft where the encoder used for velocity control is mounted.</p>\r\n<p>If there is only one encoder configured, or if the encoder used for position control is on the motor shaft, this parameter is not used. To scale the position between the driving shaft and the output of a gearbox, 0x6092 Feed constant should be used to create a virtual gear ratio instead.</p>\r\n<p>All values for this parameter are dimensionless.</p>",
                    "inputType": "number",
                    "isSmm": false,
                    "bitSize": 64,
                    "esiType": "DT6091ARR",
                    "canBeMappedAsRxPdo": true,
                    "canBeMappedAsTxPdo": false,
                    "recordDescription": "",
                    "options": "",
                    "group": "Gear ratio",
                    "typeValue": "",
                    "originalOptions": "",
                    "value": 1,
                    "readOnly": false
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
